I'd certainly agree with that. But if you're going to be able to cast
magic mapping once every four or five mazes (Pw of 40 or 50, say, and
50% failure rate), and that's the only high-level spell you care about
casting, it may be a better use of resources to just use the extra 30
marker charges, especially if it also costs marker charges to get your
HoB up to +5, your robe enchanted and fixed, &c. It always depends on
the individual resources you have that game, unless you farm or polypile
until you have all the resources you could possibly want. Even then,
you need to write the charging scrolls for your polymorph wand(s),
unless you get lucky.

If I had a spellbook of magic mapping, of course I would read it, and 
take reasonable steps toward being able to cast it. But I can easily
imagine situations where it wouldn't be worth the effort to seek out
and learn the spell. Of course, in some of those situations, I've 
gone and done it anyway, because the incidental other spells are nice. :)

